  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to Landslide in Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 24 May 2024, a significant landslide occurred in Maip Muritaka Rural Local-Level Government (LLG) in Lagaip-Porgera district, leading to extensive damage and fatalities, impacting six villages in Yambali ward with an estimated population of 3,895 people, after a large number of debris was dislodged from Mount Mungalo. Through this proposed project, IOM will contribute towards mitigating the impacts of the Mulitaka Landslide in Enga Province through the delivery of lifesaving assistance to affected populations. In collaboration with the Provincial Disaster Coordination Office (PDCO) and the Disaster Management Team, IOM will expand its services to meet the Shelter, Food and Health/MHPSS needs of communities affected by landslides. The assistance will target 2000 of the most vulnerable individuals in Enga province, with emphasis on the most vulnerable persons, such as women, persons living with disability, and older people. The interventions will help to facilitate Internally Displaced Persons (IDP) return, where feasible and safe, and improve living conditions in the villages of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
